  heard in that clip talking more about  business taxes and corporation tax  that's something that's also been  focused on by other leadership  contenders other people like nadeem  zahari and suella braveman have also  made a big play for their tax cutting  credentials now why are they doing this  well i think the strategy is on this  part anyway that because they are  appealing not necessarily to the general  public but to tory mps and tory members  the the logic is  if you say you'll cut taxes then you'll  get votes well yes to an extent but i  think competence also matters in all of  this that's to say i think the people  voting the rank and file tory card  carrying members around the country have  got to believe that you're able to make  your sums add up and that you can pay  for some of these tax rises and bluntly  we're already hearing quite a lot of  shade thrown on some of these claims the  ifs the institute for fiscal studies  which is pretty down the line on this  sort of stuff a team of economists that  scrutinizes the government's work its  boss paul johnson has already said today  that if we are going to have tax cuts of  some of these levels then people need to  be honest that it means things like  public pay not keeping up with rising  prices so real terms cuts for people  that work in the public sector or it  means more borrowing which would go  against potentially conservative  manifesto  promises i think as well what appeals to  conservative party members and mps  doesn't necessarily win votes in the  broader public and i think whilst you  can make a pretty good argument for  cutting business taxes and corporation  tax if the first thing a new prime  minister did in the middle of a cost of  living crisis was dropped taxes for  businesses i think bluntly the labour  party would be licking their lips at  that prospect in terms of new entrants  we've had today penny mordant an  international trade minister has become  the ninth person to enter the race she's  posted quite a patriotic video um online  on twitter saying it needs to be  less about the leader and more about the  ship penny morton of course has a  military  background she's also been quite keen to  get on the front foot  and dispel as she sees it anyway some  issues around sort of identity politics  and gender identity that she has come  under fire for um in the past as i say a  tenth candidate liz trust will likely  announce in the next 24 hours expect as  well as tax another big issue to  potentially be  the candidates relationships and how  close they were with boris johnson we're  already starting to get a sense of that  in the interviews this morning jeremy  hunt being pretty clear about um his uh  distaste shall we say for the pr for the  current interim prime minister uh on the  way out um in the coming weeks grant  shaps on the other hand talking up uh  essentially boris johnson and saying his  problem may have been that he was too  loyal and talking up essentially his  credentials as someone that stuck with  the prime minister and didn't spend a  lot of time plotting now i think we are  certainly going to get to 10 candidates  there have been people tweeting support  for the home secretary pretty patel  overnight so we may well go even higher  than 10 it will be for senior  conservative mps that set the rules on  this leadership race tomorrow to decide  whether they want to tighten the rules  and compress the leadership contest to  try and whittle those candidates down to  two in a quick way
 

